Negative control for the visible column set being URL STATE (`R6-25`).

Holds the set in a component-local ref instead of the playground's one query
writer. On screen it looks identical — the picker ticks and un-ticks, the header
row follows — and the whole capability the ruling asked for is gone: nothing
round-trips, nothing pastes, and a colleague opening the link lands on a
different table from the one he was sent to. This is the shape a picker written
without reading `R6-25` naturally takes.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the column-set spec — a `columns=` param no longer decides which headers
are drawn, and hiding a column no longer writes one, so the round-trip cases
fail. The default-set and options cases stay green, which is what keeps the
mutation honest about which law it withdraws.

